{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "So sorry to bother you with this, but could you please point us to the steps for routing incoming lab results to whatever covering physician is on duty? We are so sorry for any confusion on our end, we just want to make sure these signed and annotated reports end up in the right hands.",
   "id": "gen-111",
   "subject": "Question regarding lab result routing to covering providers"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am terribly sorry to bug support with this, but I am trying to clear out a few medication alerts for a patient where the preferred drug is currently out of stock at their pharmacy. I went into the prescription module and clicked on the substitution option, but the system keeps looping me back to the primary medication screen instead of letting me select an alternative therapeutic agent. I have tried clearing my browser cache and restarting the session, but it still happens. Could you please advise how we are supposed to handle these pharmacy substitution messaging workflows? So sorry again for taking up your time.",
   "id": "gen-112",
   "subject": "Apologies - having trouble with out-of-stock medication substitutions"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, we need a little guidance on attaching scanned paper files to patient records. When we try to upload oversized outside PDF reports, the system throws a generic processing error. Could you let us know what the maximum file size limit is and the best way to handle these documents?",
   "id": "gen-113",
   "subject": "Help with uploading outside lab reports"
  },
  {
   "body": "To Whom It May Concern,\n\nWe are currently in the process of building custom intake forms and medical history questionnaires for our patients to complete prior to their scheduled appointments. However, when publishing the form layout, we encounter persistent field validation errors on the date of birth and emergency contact fields, preventing successful deployment. Kindly advise on the proper configuration parameters to resolve this issue.\n\nSincerely,\nPractice Administration",
   "id": "gen-114",
   "subject": "Inquiry Regarding Digital Intake Form Field Validation Errors"
  },
  {
   "body": "So sorry to bother you, but it looks like our latest monthly subscription invoice has an incorrect charge on it. Could someone please review our account and refund the extra amount?",
   "id": "gen-115",
   "subject": "Billing discrepancy on monthly invoice"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi there, we are getting ready to batch our insurance claims for the clearinghouse today and wanted to know the quickest way to check for validation errors beforehand. Thanks.",
   "id": "gen-116",
   "subject": "Claim generation and validation check"
  },
  {
   "body": "To Support,\n\nI am writing to report a serious privacy concern regarding an electronic lab order sent out this morning. During the transmission process for patient J.D., the interface appeared to briefly display demographic and diagnostic details belonging to a completely different individual from an afternoon slot. Given the strict nature of data privacy regulations, we are quite concerned about this breach of confidentiality and require an immediate investigation into how this crossover occurred.\n\nRegards,\nPractice Administrator",
   "id": "gen-117",
   "subject": "URGENT: Potential cross-patient data exposure during lab order transmission"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, we are trying to get some outside paper lab reports attached to patient charts today. Every time we try to bring in the scanned PDF files, the upload seems to stall out. Is there a specific size limit we should be aware of?",
   "id": "gen-118",
   "subject": "Attaching scanned paper reports to charts"
  },
  {
   "body": "We keep getting rejections on electronic lab orders due to ICD-10 code mismatches. How do we quickly fix and re-transmit these orders without rebuilding the entire test panel from scratch? Please advise.",
   "id": "gen-119",
   "subject": "Lab order rejections and diagnosis codes"
  },
  {
   "body": "I am terribly sorry to drop this on you right now while my waiting room is completely full, but I desperately need to pull the security audit logs to see who accessed a specific patient chart this morning. Patients are waiting and I am under immense pressure. Could you please walk me through exporting these logs immediately? So sorry for the rush.",
   "id": "gen-120",
   "subject": "So sorry - urgent need to access security audit logs with patients waiting"
  }
 ]
}
